{{Quote|Buzz is a lifeguard at the Velocirapids water park and a real stickler for the rules. He clearly enjoys wielding the tiny bit of authority he has to the greatest degree possible.}}{{Portrait}}
Buzz is a {{Rarity|Mythic}} [[Brawler]] who could be unlocked as a [[Brawl Pass]] reward at Tier 30 in Season 7: Jurassic Splash. He has high health, a high damage output, a very fast reload speed, and great mobility because of his Super and his fast movement speed, but a short attack range. He was the 48th Brawler added to the game. His Trait allows him to passively charge his Super if an enemy Brawler is within a radius of him. He attacks with close-ranged sound waves from his whistle. His Super throws out a buoy that can grapple walls or enemies, pulling him to them and stunning nearby enemies with the stun duration varying based on his travel distance. His first Gadget, Reserve Buoy, instantly and fully charges his Super with this Super not stunning enemies. His second Gadget, X-Ray-Shades, momentarily allows Buzz and his teammates to see enemies hiding in bushes within his Trait's Super charging area. His first Star Power, Tougher Torpedo, doubles the minimum stun duration of his Super. His second Star Power, Eyes Sharp, increases his Trait's area to cover more ground. His Hypercharge, Buzzwatch, recharges Buzz's Super instantly when he hits a wall.

==Trait==
{{Quote|This Brawler charges Super from staying close to opposing enemies.}}{{Trait|Radius}}Buzz's Trait is a 6-tile circle around him. All enemy Brawlers within this circle charge his Super. He charges his Super and Hypercharge faster if there are multiple enemies inside the radius, and the amount of Super charge per second is 3.375% multiplied by one more than the number of enemies present within the circle. This results in the Super charging by 6.75% per second each or over 15 seconds for one enemy, and his Hypercharge by 1.6875% per second each or over 60 seconds for one enemy. His Super and Hypercharge still charge even with invisible or bush-camping enemies. Ally Buzzes will have their Trait radius shown, while enemy Buzzes will have their Trait radius hidden.

==Attack: Buzz Off==
{{Quote|Buzz blows on his lifeguard whistle, piercing nearby ears five times in an arc.}}Buzz blows 5 close-ranged, piercing sound waves from his whistle in a strafing motion from left to right. His attack has a slow unload speed, taking 0.9 seconds to complete.

==Super: Torpedo Throw==
{{Quote|Buzz throws out his torpedo buoy. If it hits an opponent or a wall, Buzz hauls himself over there, stunning nearby opponents where he lands. The stun time increases based on distance travelled.}}Buzz throws out a buoy that can hit both opposing targets or walls, pulling himself to it afterwards. After Buzz pulls to an enemy, he stuns them and other enemies in a 2.33-tile radius around himself. The stun duration is variable; the farther away Buzz was before hitting a target with his Super, the longer the stun duration. The maximum stun duration is 1.5 seconds and the minimum is 0.6 seconds. If Buzz moves behind an obstacle while using his Super, he goes through the obstacle. If the grappled enemy moves away from where they were initially hit, Buzz is pulled to their original location. Buzz can travel across lakes while being pulled, he can still move before the buoy hits an enemy or wall, and if a wall Buzz grappled onto gets destroyed, he'll be pulled to the wall's location. However, Buzz's Super can be interrupted if he's pulled, stunned, pushed back, or knocked back while using his Super.

==Gadgets==
===Reserve Buoy===
{{Quote|Instantly fills the Super meter, but the next Torpedo Throw doesn't stun opponents. Cooldown: 18 seconds.}}{{Gadget|1}}When Buzz activates this Gadget, he charges his Super instantly, but this Super won't stun enemies. Buzz can't use this Gadget if his Super is already charged, and if he gets defeated before he uses that Super, Buzz respawns without the Gadget's Super. A Gadget symbol will glow above Buzz's head signaling this Gadget's usage, as well as a glowing Super joystick. This Gadget's cooldown starts after the button is pressed.

===X-Ray-Shades===
{{Quote|Buzz can see into all bushes in his Super charging area for 12 seconds. Cooldown: 20 seconds.}}{{Gadget|2}}Upon activation, this Gadget allows Buzz and allies to see every enemy hiding in bushes within his Trait's Super charging area for the next 12 seconds. Buzz's Eyes Sharp Star Power affects the radius of this Gadget. However, if Buzz is defeated, the effect is cut short. A Gadget symbol will glow above Buzz's head signaling this Gadget's usage. This Gadget's cooldown begins after the active duration of the Gadget ends.

==Star Powers==
===Tougher Torpedo===
{{Quote|The minimum duration of Buzz's Super stun is increased by 0.5 seconds.}}{{StarPower|1}}The minimum stun duration of his Super is increased to 1.1s second instead of the usual 0.6 seconds. This Star Power doesn't affect his Reserve Buoy Gadget or the maximum stun duration of his Super. 

===Eyes Sharp===
{{Quote|Buzz's Super charging area is increased by 33%.}}{{StarPower|2}}Buzz's Trait's Super charging area is much larger. Despite the description, the 33% increase is of the radius and not the area, so his Trait's radius is increased from 6 tiles to 8 tiles.

==Hypercharge: Buzzwatch==
{{Quote|Buzz's torpedo can now be used again if he hits a wall.}}{{Hypercharge}}
When activated, Buzz's Super recharges instantly when he hits a wall. This includes the Supers charged from his Reserve Buoy Gadget. He also gains a 20% speed boost, as well as a 5% damage and shield boost.

==Mutation==
{{RemovedContent|section}}
{{Quote|Buzz's Torpedo Throw has increased range.}}<div style="float:right">[[File:Mutation.png|64px|link=]]</div>Buzz's Super range was doubled.

==Wasabi Power==
